    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r01/G1",
      "evidence_sha256": "47d08a6dd18119c66aa154e7759431c483625c7d55145f7316d5780bf72d3350",
      "assessment": "R1 G1 uses useful R0-fixed quartiles and matched interval delivery: early motion increases about 20%, with no clipping, and two middle-stratum jumps dominate Mean. Yet its B-minus-A ledger flips Mean only; median, extrema and win rate remain reciprocal. It repeatedly calls Best unchanged at 7.708 although r01 Best is 7.78846. These factual errors enter memory.",
      "decision_update": "The proposals [7,5,5,5] and [6,6,5,5] are both selected for R2 as G3 and G2. They provide a legal one-tick monotonicity probe and a conditional adjacent-window probe. Preserve the separation of geometry from affinity, but use a single oriented comparison object for all statistics and read actual group Best before forecasting.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Current-state geometry at step25 has no same-step R0 comparison, as the analyst acknowledges. Its matching and subgroup summaries cannot identify the cause of the large jumps. A later shared TOP1 parent differs from the analyst source group, so absolute R0 gain is not solely the marginal edit response.",
