    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r01/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "bb56738cf0c845e6c795a55fc0cd589c8249da2c761a0811aa1ba97681768a98",
      "assessment": "R1 G2 correctly describes the early reduction as a small net loss formed from offsetting Q3 loss and Q4 gain, with actual delivery reduced and no saturation. It still reports reciprocal win rate 0.53 as latest-over-R0 (correct value 0.47), and H2 incorrectly says interval1 supplies more motion than interval0. No candidate traces support calling the residual noise or a ceiling.",
      "decision_update": "Proposes [4,5,6,5] and [4,4,5,5]; neither is selected for R2. They test new conditional windows while retaining the early reduction, but the scheduler instead retains the stronger early direction and a cleaner mid component. Record unselected hypotheses without assigning them an unobserved outcome.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The analyst explicitly withholds a variance threshold and recognises current geometry is not endpoint quality; this is a useful counterexample to blanket claims of reckless escalation. A nearly cancelling Mean does not prove the window is globally insensitive.",
